 ## Connection and room limits
 
-One address may hold `--max-conns-per-ip` connections at once, and further ones are closed right after accepting. Players behind one NAT share an address, so raise it for LAN events or carrier grade NAT.
+One address may hold `--max-conns-per-ip` connections at once, and further ones are closed right after accepting. Loopback connections (clients on the server's own host) are not capped. Players behind one NAT share an address, so raise it for LAN events or carrier grade NAT.
 
